# SABOTAGE: T76 fix round 1, MED-2 — drops the `Enum.reject(&(&1.key == other))` step from
# `activity_leaderboard/3`, leaving the primitive's own bounded-tail `Other` sentinel
# (`Samen.Web.Reads.other_key/0`, `:__other__`) eligible to rank alongside real owners. Because
# ranking sorts by count DESCENDING, the Other slice's arithmetic-remainder value — which can
# legitimately exceed any single real owner's count once discovery is capped — can rank FIRST:
# a fabricated "member" (the sentinel atom, not an actual owner_id) topping the leaderboard.
# Orgs whose activity is fully discovered (no Other tail ever materializes) stay green — exactly
# why the named test forces discovery capping via a small `discovery_limit: 2` against 4 real
# owners, engineered so the Other remainder (2) strictly exceeds each real owner's count (1).
# Reverts byte-exact.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/crm_reporting_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: MED-2 FIX: the Other tail sentinel can NEVER appear as a leaderboard row, even when its arithmetic value would outrank every real owner
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/reads.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/reads.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/reads.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/crm/reads.ex
@@ -850,8 +850,7 @@
